dx build - run Bazel build over resolved targets

run Bazel build over resolved targets

Usage: dx build|test [--here] [--debug|--release] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Arguments:
  [TARGETS]...
          Scopes to run on

  [BAZEL_OPTIONS]...
          Args after --

Options:
      --workspace <WORKSPACE>
          Use this workspace dir

      --dry-run
          Show the plan without running it

      --quiet
          Hide summaries

  -v, --verbose
          Show more logs

      --color <COLOR>
          Set color output

      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Set log level

      --output <OUTPUT>
          Set output format

      --report <REPORT>
          Write a report file

      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>
          Fail on this severity

      --min-coverage <MIN_COVERAGE>
          Require this coverage percent

      --check
          Check without changing files

      --debug
          Use debug build

      --release
          Use release build

      --bazel
          Also run bazel clean

      --pin <PIN>
          Re-pin to this version

      --rollback
          Re-pin the last release

      --configured
          Use cquery instead of query

      --from <FROM>
          Migrate from this version

      --to <TO>
          Migrate to this version

      --here
          Use the current dir tree
          
          [alias: --cwd]

      --serve
          Serve docs locally

      --port <PORT>
          Docs serve port

      --host <HOST>
          Docs serve host

      --open
          Open docs in a browser

      --offline
          Run without network
          
          [alias: --frozen]

  -h, --help
          Print help

Per-command flags: --debug | --release (build/run/test/deploy only; mutually exclusive; bare invocation means dev, except deploy means release).

Scopes: explicit Bazel labels/patterns (//..., //pkg:target, @repo//...), or workspace-relative files/dirs resolved via Bazel query. Graph-scope commands select //... when no scope is supplied. Pass --here (--cwd alias) for the current directory tree instead (//path/...; //... at the root); --here cannot be combined with explicit scopes and never changes the no-flag default.
Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage/scope/owner errors; 1 operational failures; Bazel-authoritative failures preserve Bazel's code.
Output: --output text|json; --report has no standard format for this command.

dx - Run Bazel workflows

dx <command> [flags] [scope ...] [-- bazel-options ...]

Scopes: labels, patterns, files, or dirs. No scope means //... for most commands.

Exit codes: 0 success, 2 usage error, 1 failed check.

Usage: dx [COMMAND]

Commands:
  security    run security audit over resolved scopes (non-mutating; live Gitleaks plus advisory/vuln backends)
  license     run license audit over resolved scopes (non-mutating; live license-policy plus SPDX backend)
  lint        run lint analysis over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)
  typecheck   run typecheck analysis over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)
  format      check or rewrite formatting over resolved scopes (mutating by default; --check is non-mutating)
  generate    emit/sync BUILD files (Gazelle pipeline; mutating by default; --check validates without writes)
  build       run Bazel build over resolved targets
  test        run Bazel test over resolved targets
  coverage    collect LCOV coverage with optional threshold
  run         build and run runnable targets sequentially (explicit labels/patterns; file/dir scopes need exactly one runnable)
  deploy      build and run a single deployable target
  check       run format+lint+typecheck+generate checks in order (non-mutating)
  fix         apply format+lint+typecheck+generate fixes in order (mutating by default; no rerun, run `dx check` to validate)
  clean       prune unselected managed state, never Bazel outputs unless --bazel (no scopes)
  update      update dependencies per set through qualified resolvers (mutating without confirmation; --check is the preset stale gate)
  bump        widen one declared requirement to a new version (explicit; mutating without confirmation)
  migrate     rewrite breaking changes across releases (upgrade-only; mutating by default; --dry-run plans without writes)
  codegen     collect codegen outputs with atomic commit (mutating managed state)
  env         collect the managed development environment (mutating managed state)
  setup       collect setup outputs with atomic commit (mutating managed state)
  init        scaffold dx into a foreign tree (absent-only; mutating by default)
  new         scaffold a minimal qualified project for one language (absent-only; mutating by default)
  upgrade     one-shot pin+migrate+setup composition with recovery pointer (mutating by default; --dry-run plans without writes)
  hooks       manage Git hooks via hermetic Git (mutating by default)
  status      report workspace and target status
  version     report version and pin drift
  watch       watch for changes and rebuild (local only)
  owners      query owners of files via Bazel query
  deps        query dependencies of targets
  why         explain why a target depends on another
  completion  emit shell completions from the CLI grammar (bash|zsh|fish|powershell; --check verifies without writing)
  docs        build, check, and serve the unified documentation site (non-mutating; --check validates without rendering)
  bazel       forward raw arguments to the Bazel launcher

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Environment:
  DX_WORKSPACE=<dir>
      Default for --workspace.
  DX_DRY_RUN=<bool>
      Default for --dry-run.
  DX_QUIET=<bool>
      Default for --quiet.
  DX_VERBOSE=<bool>
      Default for --verbose.
  DX_COLOR=<mode>
      Default for --color.
  DX_OUTPUT=<mode>
      Default for --output.
  DX_FAIL_ON=<level>
      Default for --fail-on.
  RUST_LOG=<filter>
      Override --verbose and --log-level.
  NO_COLOR=<any>
      Disable color output.
  BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY=<dir>
      Workspace start under `bazel run`.
  .dx/config.toml
      Same defaults as the DX_ variables, below the environment.
